{#-
  Full-screen search overlay, from design-source/partials/search.html.

  Site search is BUILT (features.searchEnabled). The index is compiled at build
  time by src/search-index.11ty.js into /search-index.json and queried in the
  browser by js/site-search.js — no backend, no form, no third-party service,
  and no network work beyond one same-origin fetch of that static file.

  Progressive enhancement, the same discipline as the register keyword filter
  on /receipts/: the search box ships `hidden` and only js/site-search.js
  reveals it. With JS off a reader never sees an input that does nothing.

  THE OVERLAY IS A JS-ONLY CONTROL. `.search-ov` is `display:none` until
  js/ui.js adds `open`, so with script off it could never appear — and the
  shortcut links inside it, which the overlay's whole fallback story rested on,
  were never rendered to anyone. tools/behaviour_checks.py measured exactly
  that: "only 0 of 9 link blocks rendered". So:

    - /search/ (src/search.njk) is a real page carrying the same destinations
      as ordinary page markup, and the header control is now a real link to it
      (partials/header.njk). With script off, the control navigates.
    - This element ships the `search-ov--nojs` class and NO dialog semantics.
      js/ui.js removes the class and adds role/aria-modal/aria-label, so the
      thing is a dialog only where a dialog can actually open. With script off
      it stays an ordinary in-flow block of the same destinations, which is
      what makes those links rendered rather than merely present.
    - CSS REQUIRED for that state (integration.css, not written here — stream
      C16 does not own that file). Without it this element simply stays
      `display:none` with script off, exactly as it is today:
        .search-ov--nojs{position:static;display:block;background:none;z-index:auto;
                         padding:0 clamp(24px,6vw,80px) clamp(56px,10vw,120px)}
        .search-ov--nojs .so-top{display:none}
      The second rule matters: `.so-top` holds the close button, and a close
      button that cannot close anything is the dead control this whole change
      exists to remove.

  The Receipts destination is one of the same .so-links blocks rather than a
  standalone u-btn, so the overlay presents one consistent row of destinations.

  js/ui.js still owns open/close; site-search.js takes focus from the `open`
  class ui.js sets, after ui.js's own focus() for that tick.

  DESIGN: structure fixed. CONTENT: shortcuts from _data/chrome.json.
-#}
<div class="search-ov search-ov--nojs">
  <div class="so-top">{% image "logos/logo-tight-light.png", "", "8rem", [160, 320], "lazy", "logo-44" %}<button class="drawer-x" type="button" aria-label="Close search" data-search-close>&#10005;</button></div>
  {% if features.searchEnabled %}
  <div class="so-search" data-search-box hidden>
    <label for="site-search">Search uncost.org</label>
    <input id="site-search" type="search" placeholder="Try &ldquo;shelter&rdquo; or &ldquo;pledge&rdquo;&hellip;" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="site-search-status">
    <p class="so-status" id="site-search-status" role="status" data-search-status></p>
    <ul class="so-results" data-search-results></ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="so-links"><a href="/receipts/">Search the Receipts</a>{% for link in chrome.searchShortcuts %}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</div>
</div>
<script src="/js/site-search.js" defer></script>
